# UST.G3EU: H02 Component-16 Recovery-Basis Mismatch Audit Theorem

## Statement

Let `M16` be the exact `1238 x 1221` component-16 reduced presentation over
`Q(gamma)`, and let `M1200` be the certified independent 1,200-row subsystem.
The first checkpoint recovery is **not** a kernel of `M1200`.

The interrupted FLINT serialization fixed 400 coordinate rows of a 21-column
kernel basis. The rejected recovery completed those rows after imposing the
identity on coordinates `986..1006`. Exact replay on the 400 selected
complement equations and the 38 omitted equations gives:

```text
audited equations                 438
defective equations               120
defects inside M1200              101
defects among the 38 omitted       19
nonzero residual slots           2072
```

Because 101 certified subsystem equations fail literally over `Q(gamma)`, the
archive is rejected before any residual-rank promotion.

## Cause

The two 21-element coordinate sets were conflated:

```text
incorrect imposed free set: 986,987,...,1006

standard nullspace free set:
1199,1200,1201,1202,1204,1205,...,1220
```

The first set is the finite relation-coordinate block retained by the G3EL
reduction. It is a valid choice of free coordinates for constructing a new
normalized kernel, but it is not the basis used by the already serialized
FLINT checkpoint. Reusing the checkpoint while imposing that different
identity basis overdetermined the reconstruction inconsistently.

At the proof fiber `(p,gamma)=(21817,5)`, left-to-right elimination detects the
second displayed set as the standard free-column profile. Its complementary
800-coordinate block has rank 800 at that specialization, hence the selected
exact minor is nonzero over `Q(gamma)` and supports a corrected recovery.

## Rank-four campaign

Four fresh omitted-row specializations of the rejected archive all had rank
four. That observation remains a correct computation **about the rejected
archive's 38-row slice**, but it is not a bound on the kernel of `M1200` and is
not a component-16 rank theorem. G3EU therefore retires that campaign as a
promotion source.

This distinction is essential: repeated finite-field ranks can supply an exact
lower bound only after the displayed vectors are first proved to lie in the
kernel whose residual map is being studied.

## Corrected route

The corrected recovery must:

1. preserve the 400 complete checkpoint coordinate rows;
2. impose identity on the standard 21-column free profile;
3. solve the certified complementary `800 x 800` system exactly;
4. replay the other 400 selected equations literally;
5. replay all 38 omitted equations;
6. promote a residual rank only after steps 4 and 5 pass their stated checks.

The corrected solve is a new candidate, not a repair by assertion. Until its
full replay succeeds, component 16 remains at the previously certified finite
rank 138 with characteristic-zero upper rank 159, and the global H02 interval
remains `4748..5102`.

